Sval: a dialog under a Quick Peek waits for the keyboard

A Quick Peek is drawn over its owner tab, which stays selected and keeps
running. A dialog that tab's page opens, such as a prompt(), is hidden behind
the Quick Peek, and SubDialogManager focused it all the same, so what the
user typed for the page in the Quick Peek went to a box they could not see
and back to the page that opened it. The dialog is left unfocused while a
Quick Peek covers its tab, and SvalQuickPeek focuses it on closing.

diff --git a/toolkit/modules/SubDialog.sys.mjs b/toolkit/modules/SubDialog.sys.mjs
index a2c8c12e70..a59ea38ab4 100644
--- a/toolkit/modules/SubDialog.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/modules/SubDialog.sys.mjs
@@ -1151,7 +1151,16 @@ export class SubDialogManager {
   _onDialogOpen(dialog) {
     let lowerDialogs = [];
     if (dialog == this._topDialog) {
-      dialog.focus(true);
+      // Sval: a Quick Peek covers the tab under it and has the keyboard, so
+      // that tab's dialog takes focus when the Quick Peek closes
+      // (SvalQuickPeek.sys.mjs).
+      if (
+        !this._dialogStack.matches(
+          "#tabbrowser-tabpanels[sval-quick-peek] > :not(.sval-quick-peek-panel) *"
+        )
+      ) {
+        dialog.focus(true);
+      }
     } else {
       // Opening dialog is not on top, hide it
       lowerDialogs.push(dialog);
